  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work each piece in dk yarn using a 3.5 mm hook and a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring-a71"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " start. Stuff each piece firmly before closing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Head"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "21-round sphere, 8 cm diameter. Fit safety eyes between rounds 8 and 9, about 3 sts apart. Stuff firmly and close."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Body"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Oval body, 8 cm long and 12 cm wide. Stuff firmly and leave a tail for sewing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Legs (make 4)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Capsule leg, 3 cm wide and 5 cm long. Use a contrasting colour for the bottom 3 rounds to suggest hooves."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Horn"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cone horn, 2 cm base and 5 cm tall. Work in a pale gold or yellow yarn. Do not stuff."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ears (make 2)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Small cone, 2 cm base and 3 cm tall. Work in white. Do not stuff."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assembly"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pin and sew the head to the top front of the body. Attach the four legs to the underside so the unicorn stands level. Sew the horn to the centre front of the head above the eyes. Pin the ears on either side of the horn base and sew in place."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Mane and tail"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cut lengths of pink, lilac, or mint yarn, each about 15 cm long. Fold each length in half and pull the loop through a stitch using a crochet hook, then pass the tails through the loop to form a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "yarn-mane-a71"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "yarn mane"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Work mane stitches from the base of the horn back along the neck to the body join. Repeat for the tail at the back of the body. Trim to an even length."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "invisible-decrease-a71"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "invisible decrease"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " throughout for a smooth surface. Weave in all ends. Embroider nostrils in pink satin stitch just above the muzzle if desired."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Materials needed"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Approximately 36 g white dk yarn, small amounts of gold and pink yarn for horn and mane. Pair of 10 mm safety eyes. Polyester stuffing. Tapestry needle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to make next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The amigurumi dragon uses a similar body construction with added wings and cone spines along the back."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
